THOUGHT: NullAway complains because loadData is nullable and dereferenced without a check in onDataReady. The pattern used in cancel() shows the intended safe access: copy loadData to a local variable, check for null, and only then use it. I’ll mirror that pattern in onDataReady, and then run the NullAway build to confirm that exactly one error is removed and no new ones are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/glide && sed -i '131,134c\  @Override
  public void onDataReady(@Nullable Object data) {
    LoadData<?> local = loadData;
    if (local != null) {
      cb.onDataFetcherReady(
          sourceKey, data, local.fetcher, DataSource.RESOURCE_DISK_CACHE, currentKey);
    }
  }' library/src/main/java/com/bumptech/glide/load/engine/ResourceCacheGenerator.java && ./gradlew library:compileDebugJavaWithJavac -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

